response:
Check Point reported critical directory traversal vulnerabilities in WinRAR affecting versions on Windows. A malicious archive named zakon.rar was observed executing PowerShell scripts. The vulnerabilities (CVE-2018-20250, CVE-2018-20251, CVE-2018-20252, CVE-2018-20253) allow attackers to extract files into arbitrary folders like the Windows Startup directory. The issue was patched in WinRAR 5.70 Beta 1.

